{
  "version": "1.0.1",
  "notes": "Added modem_power_cycle_test.py: a bench test to validate whether the modem can be fully powered down (AT+CPOWD=1) between logging cycles to save power, and reliably wake back up via the existing reset() sequence -- BEFORE trusting that in the unattended automatic logging flow (auto_log.py). Right now nothing powers the modem down between cycles at all; it stays fully powered and registered/idle-searching continuously, which likely draws more current than the Pico's own always-awake loop. AT+CPOWD is a real power-off though, not a soft reset -- many SIM7600 modules need their PWRKEY pin toggled to power back on, which may or may not be what config.py's PIN_MODEM_RESET is actually wired to on this board. Run this test first (with a PC connected, ready to physically power-cycle the modem if it doesn't come back) to find out safely before any of this gets wired into the automatic flow.",
